On Thursday, 6 June 2024 at 17:59, Harry Fallows <harryfallows@protonmail.c=
om.INVALID> wrote:

> Hi everyone,
>=20
> I would like to propose a change to allow the static configuration of lea=
der and follower replication throttling rates.
>=20
> These configurations are very useful for preventing client traffic from g=
etting throttled by replication traffic during events that cause a spike in=
 replication. Currently they are only configurable dynamically, which means=
 they are only really useful for throttling replication traffic during plan=
ned events. By allowing these configurations to be set statically, they can=
 be used to prevent client traffic throttling during unplanned events.
>=20
> KIP: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1051%3A+Static=
ally+configured+log+replication+throttling
>=20
> Best regards,
