Hi Edoardo,

Yes, you're completely right that this is a health check for the runtime,
not for specific connectors/tasks. The gap that this is meant to address
(which is not covered by the existing status endpoints for
connectors/tasks) is that endpoints related to the
creation/reconfiguration/deletion/etc. of connectors can become unavailable
on a worker, but in a way that doesn't prevent the status endpoints from
being queried, or connectors/tasks that were already assigned to the worker
from running. If this health check endpoint reports that the worker is
healthy, it means that those endpoints should also be available.

Cheers,

Chris

