Hey Wojciech,

It has been a long time since we did the jump but we had wai=
ted until 3=2E3=2Ex release when we did the jump and there were a lot of ma=
nual steps at that time=2E We then had another manual step when going to ei=
ther 3=2E4 or 3=2E5 don't remember which but that one was easier cause we d=
id have the option to turn off every broker and kraft server at once to do =
that one safely=2E I would suggest going from 2=2E6=2E2 to 3=2E6=2E2 and th=
en stopping and waiting until 3=2E7=2E1 comes out as there is a pretty seri=
ous flaw in 3=2E7=2E0=2E And I would suggest probably seeing what the offic=
ial migration guides have to say because my understanding is that the bulk =
of the changes since we started the migration is around making sure it is a=
 smooth and safe upgrade process overall=2E

The other option that you coul=
d always do (our fallback plan) is to spinup a brand new cluster and to cop=
y all the topics from the old cluster to the new cluster=2E Tedious and tak=
es several days depending on how much data you have but it is safe and work=
s as well=2E

Sorry I don't know what are all of the options and a lot has =
changed since we had to do the hard step of going from 2 to 3=2E Once on 3=
=2Ex, the upgrades have been pretty smooth=2E

