> are committed to getting it right with help and feedback from the Kafk=
a=20
> community.=20
> For example, on ensuring plugin compatibility, one of the important=20
> points brought up in our discussions was around how clients would=20
> obtain the correct plugin versions for a particular client language an=
d=20
> plugin version. We=E2=80=99d like to see a process where registration =
of the=20
> plugins with the Kafka cluster also facilitates distribution of the=20
> correct plugin versions to the clients.  When registering a new plugin=20
> with Kafka, the process would have the admin upload metadata and the=20
> corresponding plugins for each language client into language-specific=20
> internal topics. When a new client connects to the cluster, it could=20
> query available plugins from an internal topic, then download the=20
> correct plugin for itself from the correct topic holding binaries or=20
> plugin code for that language. This tight coupling would ensure that=20
> any client connecting to the plugin-enabled Kafka could either continu=
e=20
> to use existing codecs or obtain the required compression codec plugin=
s=20
