Goufu created KAFKA-16996:
-----------------------------

             Summary: The leastLoadedNode() function in kafka-client may ch=
oose a faulty node during the consumer thread starting and meanwhile one of=
 the KAFKA server node is dead.
                 Key: KAFKA-16996
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16996
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: clients
    Affects Versions: 3.6.0, 2.3.0, 2.0.1
            Reporter: Goufu


The leastLoadedNode() function has a bug during the consumer process starti=
ng period. The function sendMetadataRequest() called by getTopicMetadataReq=
uest() uses a random node which maybe faulty since every node=E2=80=98s sta=
te recorded in the client thread is not ready yet. It happened in my produc=
tion environment during my consumer thread restarting and meanwhile one of =
the KAFKA server node is dead.

I'm using the kafka-client-2.0.1.jar. I have checked the source code of hig=
her versions and the issue still exists.



