             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Wish
    Affects Versions: 3.7.0
            Reporter: Jianbin Chen


After enabling tiered storage, occasional residual logs are left in the rep=
lica.
Based on the observed phenomenon, the index values of the rolled-out logs g=
enerated by the replica and the leader are not the same. As a result, the l=
ogs uploaded to S3 at the same time do not include the corresponding log fi=
les on the replica side, making it impossible to delete the local logs.
